    "answer": {
      "short": "Bob’s starting equation is not an identity. Coefficients can be equated only when the equality holds for every value of $x$.",
      "worked": "The equality $(1+x)^4=(1+x)^3$ does not hold for every value of $x$. For example, at $x=1$, the left side is $16$ and the right side is $8$. Equating corresponding coefficients is valid for a polynomial identity, so Bob cannot conclude that $6=3$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
